### ============================================================
###  0. AUTH — registro y login
### ============================================================

### 0.1 · Registrar usuario normal (solo si la BBDD está vacía, si usas el seed sáltate esto)
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nombre": "Paco",
  "apellidos": "García López",
  "email": "paco@test.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "passwordConfirm": "password123",
  "cycle": "DAW"
}

###

### 0.2 · Login usuario normal → copia el access_token en @userToken (línea 7)
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "paco@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### ROL ADMIN NO VA AUUUUUNNN

### 0.3 · Login admin → copia el access_token en @adminToken (línea 8)
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 0.4 · Login con contraseña incorrecta → debe devolver 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "paco@test.com",
  "password": "contraseñaMal"
}

###

### 0.5 · Login con email inexistente → debe devolver 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "noexiste@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

###

### 0.6 · Login con body incompleto → debe devolver 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "paco@test.com"
}

###

### ============================================================
###  1. GET /api/challenges — público con paginación
### ============================================================

### 1.1 · Todos los retos (página 1, 10 por defecto)
GET {{baseUrl}}/challenges
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 1.2 · Página 2 con 5 por página
GET {{baseUrl}}/challenges?page=2&limit=5
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 1.3 · Solo la primera página con 3 resultados
GET {{baseUrl}}/challenges?page=1&limit=3
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ============================================================
###  2. GET /api/challenges/featured — público
### ============================================================

### 2.1 · Top 5 más completados (solo validados)
GET {{baseUrl}}/challenges/featured
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ============================================================
###  3. GET /api/challenges/:id — protegido (JWT)
### ============================================================

### 3.1 · Obtener reto por ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 3.2 · Sin token → debe devolver 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ============================================================
###  4. POST /api/challenges — protegido (JWT), creatorId del token
### ============================================================

### 4.1 · Crear reto (el creatorId lo coge del token automáticamente)
# @name createChallenge
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Crear número de teléfono",
  "statement": "Dada una lista de 10 dígitos, devuelve un string con formato de número de teléfono válido.",
  "dificultyId": 1,
  "languageId": 1,
  "subjectId": 2,
  "validate": false
}

### 👉 Copia el id de la respuesta y pégalo en @challengeId (línea 9)

###

### 4.2 · Sin token → debe devolver 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Sin auth",
  "statement": "Esto no debería crearse.",
  "dificultyId": 1,
  "languageId": 1,
  "subjectId": 1
}

###

### 4.3 · Body incompleto → debe devolver 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Solo título, falta todo lo demás"
}

###

### ============================================================
###  5. PATCH /api/challenges/:id — solo ADMIN
### ============================================================

### 5.1 · Admin valida el reto (validate: true)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "validate": true
}

###

### 5.2 · Admin actualiza título y dificultad
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Crear número de teléfono (v2)",
  "dificultyId": 2
}

###

### 5.3 · Usuario normal intenta hacer PATCH → debe devolver 403
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "No debería poder editar"
}

###

### 5.4 · Sin token → debe devolver 401
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Tampoco"
}

###

### ============================================================
###  6. DELETE /api/challenges/:id — solo ADMIN
### ============================================================

### 6.1 · Crear un reto para borrar
POST {{baseUrl}}/challenges
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Reto para borrar",
  "statement": "Este reto se va a eliminar en la siguiente request.",
  "dificultyId": 1,
  "languageId": 1,
  "subjectId": 1
}

###

### 6.2 · Admin borra el reto
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 6.3 · Borrar reto inexistente → debe devolver 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/challenges/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### 6.4 · Usuario normal intenta borrar → debe devolver 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/challenges/{{challengeId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ============================================================
###  7. FLUJO COMPLETO — prueba de featured tras validar
### ============================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/challenges/featured
Content-Type: application/json

###
